            <h1>⚪ Saline and Alkaline Soil – Brief Information</h1>
            <br>


            <img src="https://tse4.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.iVuBMWvqyn--BsfI5Uz8KQHaFL?pid=Api&P=0&h=180"><br>

            <b>✅ What is Saline and Alkaline Soil?</b>
            <p>
                Saline and alkaline soil contains excess salts that reduce soil fertility 
                and make crop growth difficult.
            </p>

            <br>

            <b>📍 Where is it Found in India?</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Rajasthan</li>
                <li>Gujarat</li>
                <li>Punjab</li>
                <li>Haryana</li>
                <li>Uttar Pradesh</li>
                <li>Coastal regions of India</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🎨 Colour and Appearance</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Usually white crust appears on the surface</li>
                <li>Hard and less porous</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🧪 Composition</b>
            <ul>
                <li>High salt content</li>
                <li>Low nitrogen and organic matter</li>
                <li>Poor fertility</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🌾 Crops That Can Grow</b>
            <p>(Only salt-tolerant crops)</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Barley</li>
                <li>Cotton</li>
                <li>Sugar beet</li>
                <li>Some grasses</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>⚠️ Problems</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Poor plant growth</li>
                <li>Water absorption becomes difficult</li>
                <li>Soil becomes hard and infertile</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🛠️ Improvement Methods</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Proper drainage system</li>
                <li>Adding gypsum or lime</li>
                <li>Using organic manure</li>
                <li>Flushing salts with good irrigation</li>
            </ul>

        </section>

    </div>

